===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{alternative form of|en|stay-behind}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1861|author=John Hart Dunne|title=From Calcutta to Pekin|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=jnwBAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA95&dq=%22stay+behinds%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=YgtDUcf5OZDckgXckYAg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behinds%22&f=false|page=95
|passage=Pleasant prospect for us, who are sure to be amongst the unlucky '''stay behinds'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992|author=David Drake; Bill Fawcett|title=Battlestation|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=psdUzp-ihSQC&q=%22stay+behinds%22&dq=%22stay+behinds%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=YgtDUcf5OZDckgXckYAg&redir_esc=y|page=134
|passage=“{{...}}Think there may be some bugs left. Deserters, '''stay behinds''', whatever.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|month=September|author=Scott Berinato; Chandra Tallman|chapter=The Art of Securing Pricelessness|title=CSO|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=BGAEAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA43&dq=%22stay+behinds%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=4_pCUd2SKYbfkAWyuIHYAQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behinds%22&f=false|page=43
|passage=That creates very few “dead spots” for potential thieves to avoid sensors and helps deter “'''stay behinds'''”: skulkers who come into the room with a group but remain when others leave.}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{&lit|en|stay|behind}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Effective Cycling|edition=6th|page=393|url=https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0262560704|author=John Forester|year=1993|passage=If you can, sprint ahead and stay ahead — otherwise slow down and '''stay''' well '''behind'''}}
#* '''1995''', Rudolf Steiner, Helen Fox (original translator), revising translator not named, ''Lecture 7'', ''The Kingdom of Childhood'', Revised Translation, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=181yvCb9-x4C&pg=PA120&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school&hl=en&sa=X&ei=UylAUd6zF8fEkQW_xIDYCw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school&f=false page 120],
#*: Children who are in any way below standard come into this class from all the other classes.
#*: Otherwise, as I have said, we do not let the children '''stay behind''' but we try to bring them along with us under all circumstances, so that in this way each child really receives what is right for his or her particular age.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=Helen Horne; Sally A. Brown|title=500 Tips for School Improvement|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XEszifI7UwUC&pg=PA74&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false|page=74
|passage=Teamwork is important throughout any school organisation. When people work in isolation, they tend to '''stay behind''' a closed door, locked in with their pupils.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[remain]] where one is, whilst others [[leave]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Al Kelly|title=Challenging Modern Physics: Questioning Einstein's Relativity Theories|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XVLmihZnsvUC&pg=PA24&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-BhAUfGVLoWPkAXmo4HICA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22&f=false|page=24
|passage=If a twin goes off on a spaceship for a long trip at nearly the speed of light, that twin would be much younger on return to earth than the twin who '''stayed behind''' (Fock, 1964; French, 1968; Hawking, 1988; Young, 1992).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=David W. P. Elliott|title=The Vietnamese War: Revolution and Social Change in the Mekong Delta, 1930-1975|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=JcUpuSZ5Cg8C&pg=PA91&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-BhAUfGVLoWPkAXmo4HICA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22&f=false|page=91
|passage=Much as Tra wanted to '''stay behind''', as commander of the region, it was his duty to organize and lead the troops going to the North.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=A. Dirk Moses|title=Empire, Colony, Genocide: Conquest, Occupation, and Subaltern Resistance in World History|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=q5C3Sbe1iMoC&pg=PA114&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-BhAUfGVLoWPkAXmo4HICA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22&f=false|page=114
|passage=Ross's fortunes differed sharply from those of the principal Choctaw chief, Greenwood LeFlore, who, unlike Ross, signed a removal treaty on behalf of his people, only to '''stay behind''' himself, accept US citizenship, and go on to a distinguished career in Mississippi politics.}}
# To remain in a classroom or school at the end of teaching, especially to receive punishment.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1964|author=[[w:Paul Keres|Paul Keres]]; [[w:Alexander Kotov|Alexander Kotov]]|translator=[[w:Harry Golombek|Harry Golombek]]|title=The Art of the Middle Game|year_published=1989|publisher=Dover|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=2kOO3Hv8zLsC&pg=PA32&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false|page=32
|passage=When I '''stayed behind''' at school with my school friends after lessons, and managed to play up to a hundred games in a single afternoon, the strategy was simple enough: I castled on the opposite side in the middle of violent (and mutual) King attacks.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=Louis Cohen; Lawrence Manion; Keith Morrison|title=A Guide to Teaching Practice|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XocEd8Zi5GAC&pg=PA51&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false|page=51
|passage=Observe what sanctions the teacher employs with her class in order to enforce the rules. Are individuals kept in after school, for instance, or are they asked to '''stay behind''' at the end of a lesson, or reprimanded in front of the other children?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Rebecca Mahon|title=Excel HSC English Study Guide: Billy Elliot|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ksGcdJNKb-wC&pg=PA110&dq=%22stay+behind%22%7C%22stays+behind%22%7C%22staying+behind%22%7C%22stayed+behind%22+school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0S5AUYy0K8y-kQWGu4CQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22stay%20behind%22%7C%22stays%20behind%22%7C%22staying%20behind%22%7C%22stayed%20behind%22%20school%7Cclass%7Cdetention&f=false|page=110
|passage=One day I had to '''stay behind''' after my boxing class, and I'd just been told that I was a ‘disgrace to the traditions of the boxing hall’.}}

